# DensePack 1.3
# The line endings of a new clone, on each operating system.
#
# A shell script with CRLF line endings fails on Linux and macOS. The kernel
# reads the carriage return as a part of the interpreter path on the first
# line and reports "bad interpreter: /bin/sh^M: no such file or directory".
# The same script runs when you call a shell on it by hand. For that reason,
# the fault appears only on a computer that clones the repository.
#
# Only the files that Windows runs keep CRLF. Git uses its own default for
# all other files, and no committed file changes its line endings.

*.sh text eol=lf

*.ps1 text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf

# The eval suite keeps LF on each system. A Windows clone with CRLF would give
# the agent different bytes than the published runs used.
plugin/evals/** text eol=lf

*.ttf binary
*.ttc binary
